-- title:
--   Freeness descends from M/xM along a regular element
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring that is local and Noetherian, and let $M$ be an $R$-module (an additive commutative group with an $R$-module structure) that is finite, i.e. finitely generated over $R$. Let $x \in R$ be an element of the maximal ideal of $R$ which is regular on $M$, meaning that multiplication by $x$ is injective on $M$. Suppose that the quotient $M/xM$, written `QuotSMulTop x M`, is a free module over the quotient ring $R/(x)$, where $(x)$ is the ideal generated by $x$. Then $M$ is a free $R$-module. No bound is asserted on the rank, and no hypothesis such as $x \notin \mathfrak{m}^2$ is imposed; the freeness obtained is freeness on some index type, which by the construction inside the proof may be taken to be an index set for a basis of $M/xM$ over $R/(x)$.
--
--   This is the Nakayama-type lifting of freeness along a regular element, the inductive step used in the Auslander–Buchsbaum style argument that a patched module whose depth equals the dimension of the ring is free. Within the development it is used in the study of multivariate formal groups, in [`MvFormalGroup.finite_free_finrank_quotient_span_nthSeries_of_finrank_eq_pow`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.finite_free_finrank_quotient_span_nthSeries_of_finrank_eq_pow).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Module_free_of_quotSMulTop_free.lean

import Mathlib.RingTheory.LocalRing.Module
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.StrongRankCondition
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Regular.IsSMulRegular
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Regular.RegularSequence

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open scoped Pointwise

theorem Module.free_of_quotSMulTop_free {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [IsLocalRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [Module.Finite R M] (x : R) (hx : x ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) (hreg : IsSMulRegular M x) (hfree : Module.Free (R ⧸ Ideal.span {x}) (QuotSMulTop x M)) :
    Module.Free R M := by sorry
